---
/**
 * Pretraining lesson, illustration #1.
 *
 * The transfer-learning paradigm shift: from "one model per task,
 * trained from scratch" (left) to "one pretrained base model, then
 * cheap task-specific tuning" (right). Replaces the ASCII diagram
 * inline in the lesson body with a real SVG so the size and shape
 * differences between the two paradigms are visible at a glance.
 */
---

<figure class="cw-illus">
	<svg viewBox="0 0 800 360" xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" role="img" aria-labelledby="tlp-title tlp-desc">
		<title id="tlp-title">The transfer-learning paradigm shift</title>
		<desc id="tlp-desc">A two-panel comparison. Left panel, the old paradigm: three separate small datasets (spam, sentiment, topic) each train a separate small model from scratch. Right panel, the new paradigm: one massive open-internet corpus trains a single large pretrained base model once, then three small inexpensive tuning steps adapt that one base model into a spam classifier, sentiment classifier, and topic classifier respectively. Visually, the right panel's pretraining stage is much larger than any single old-paradigm box, and the three tuning stages are much smaller; the asymmetry is the point.</desc>

		<defs>
			<marker id="cw-arrow-tlp" viewBox="0 0 10 10" refX="9" refY="5" markerWidth="8" markerHeight="8" orient="auto">
				<path d="M 0 0 L 10 5 L 0 10 z" fill="currentColor"/>
			</marker>
			<marker id="cw-arrow-tlp-accent" viewBox="0 0 10 10" refX="9" refY="5" markerWidth="8" markerHeight="8" orient="auto">
				<path d="M 0 0 L 10 5 L 0 10 z" fill="#7c3aed"/>
			</marker>
		</defs>

		<text x="180" y="28" text-anchor="middle" font-family="ui-sans-serif, system-ui, sans-serif" font-size="13" font-weight="600" fill="currentColor" opacity="0.85">Old paradigm: one model per task</text>
		<text x="600" y="28" text-anchor="middle" font-family="ui-sans-serif, system-ui, sans-serif" font-size="13" font-weight="600" fill="currentColor" opacity="0.85">New paradigm: pretrain once, tune cheaply</text>

		<line x1="380" y1="48" x2="380" y2="320" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1" stroke-dasharray="4 4" opacity="0.3"/>

		<rect x="30" y="60" width="120" height="40" rx="6" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.2" opacity="0.7"/>
		<text x="90" y="84" text-anchor="middle" font-family="ui-sans-serif, system-ui, sans-serif" font-size="11" fill="currentColor" opacity="0.85">spam dataset</text>
		<line x1="152" y1="80" x2="180" y2="80" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.2" marker-end="url(#cw-arrow-tlp)"/>
		<rect x="184" y="60" width="160" height="40" rx="6" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.2"/>
		<text x="264" y="84" text-anchor="middle" font-family="ui-sans-serif, system-ui, sans-serif" font-size="11" font-weight="600" fill="currentColor">spam model</text>

		<rect x="30" y="120" width="120" height="40" rx="6" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.2" opacity="0.7"/>
		<text x="90" y="144" text-anchor="middle" font-family="ui-sans-serif, system-ui, sans-serif" font-size="11" fill="currentColor" opacity="0.85">sentiment data</text>
		<line x1="152" y1="140" x2="180" y2="140" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.2" marker-end="url(#cw-arrow-tlp)"/>
		<rect x="184" y="120" width="160" height="40" rx="6" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.2"/>
		<text x="264" y="144" text-anchor="middle" font-family="ui-sans-serif, system-ui, sans-serif" font-size="11" font-weight="600" fill="currentColor">sentiment model</text>

		<rect x="30" y="180" width="120" height="40" rx="6" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.2" opacity="0.7"/>
		<text x="90" y="204" text-anchor="middle" font-family="ui-sans-serif, system-ui, sans-serif" font-size="11" fill="currentColor" opacity="0.85">topic dataset</text>
		<line x1="152" y1="200" x2="180" y2="200" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.2" marker-end="url(#cw-arrow-tlp)"/>
		<rect x="184" y="180" width="160" height="40" rx="6" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.2"/>
		<text x="264" y="204" text-anchor="middle" font-family="ui-sans-serif, system-ui, sans-serif" font-size="11" font-weight="600" fill="currentColor">topic model</text>

		<text x="187" y="270" text-anchor="middle" font-family="ui-sans-serif, system-ui, sans-serif" font-size="11" fill="currentColor" font-style="italic" opacity="0.6">three small models, each from scratch,</text>
		<text x="187" y="288" text-anchor="middle" font-family="ui-sans-serif, system-ui, sans-serif" font-size="11" fill="currentColor" font-style="italic" opacity="0.6">each needs its own labeled data</text>

		<rect x="410" y="55" width="180" height="56" rx="8" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.2" opacity="0.7"/>
		<text x="500" y="78" text-anchor="middle" font-family="ui-sans-serif, system-ui, sans-serif" font-size="11" fill="currentColor" opacity="0.85">the open internet</text>
		<text x="500" y="96" text-anchor="middle" font-family="ui-sans-serif, system-ui, sans-serif" font-size="10" fill="currentColor" opacity="0.6">(no labels, no annotation)</text>
		<line x1="500" y1="113" x2="500" y2="135" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.5" marker-end="url(#cw-arrow-tlp)"/>

		<rect x="410" y="138" width="380" height="60" rx="8" fill="none" stroke="#7c3aed" stroke-width="2"/>
		<text x="600" y="162" text-anchor="middle" font-family="ui-sans-serif, system-ui, sans-serif" font-size="14" font-weight="700" fill="#7c3aed">pretrained base model</text>
		<text x="600" y="182" text-anchor="middle" font-family="ui-sans-serif, system-ui, sans-serif" font-size="11" fill="currentColor" opacity="0.7">objective: predict the next token, repeated billions of times</text>

		<line x1="490" y1="200" x2="450" y2="225" stroke="#7c3aed" stroke-width="1.5" marker-end="url(#cw-arrow-tlp-accent)"/>
		<line x1="600" y1="200" x2="600" y2="225" stroke="#7c3aed" stroke-width="1.5" marker-end="url(#cw-arrow-tlp-accent)"/>
		<line x1="710" y1="200" x2="750" y2="225" stroke="#7c3aed" stroke-width="1.5" marker-end="url(#cw-arrow-tlp-accent)"/>

		<rect x="395" y="230" width="105" height="32" rx="6" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.2"/>
		<text x="447" y="251" text-anchor="middle" font-family="ui-sans-serif, system-ui, sans-serif" font-size="11" font-weight="600" fill="currentColor">tune for spam</text>

		<rect x="547" y="230" width="105" height="32" rx="6" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.2"/>
		<text x="600" y="251" text-anchor="middle" font-family="ui-sans-serif, system-ui, sans-serif" font-size="11" font-weight="600" fill="currentColor">tune for sentiment</text>

		<rect x="700" y="230" width="105" height="32" rx="6" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.2"/>
		<text x="752" y="251" text-anchor="middle" font-family="ui-sans-serif, system-ui, sans-serif" font-size="11" font-weight="600" fill="currentColor">tune for topic</text>

		<text x="600" y="288" text-anchor="middle" font-family="ui-sans-serif, system-ui, sans-serif" font-size="11" fill="currentColor" font-style="italic" opacity="0.6">one massive pretraining step, run once,</text>
		<text x="600" y="306" text-anchor="middle" font-family="ui-sans-serif, system-ui, sans-serif" font-size="11" fill="currentColor" font-style="italic" opacity="0.6">then small cheap tuning steps for any task you want</text>

		<text x="400" y="340" text-anchor="middle" font-family="ui-sans-serif, system-ui, sans-serif" font-size="12" fill="currentColor" font-style="italic" opacity="0.7">the expensive part shifts left; the per-task cost collapses</text>
	</svg>
	<figcaption>The transfer-learning paradigm shift. Old: every task is a fresh model trained from scratch on its own labeled data. New: one pretrained base model is built once on the open internet (the expensive step), and any specific task is reached by a small, cheap tuning run on top.</figcaption>
</figure>

<style>
	.cw-illus { margin: 1.75rem auto; max-width: 100%; }
	.cw-illus svg { display: block; width: 100%; max-width: 780px; height: auto; margin: 0 auto; }
	.cw-illus figcaption { text-align: center; font-size: 0.85rem; opacity: 0.75; margin-top: 0.5rem; font-style: italic; }
</style>
